  "title": "Symbols as unique keys",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## A key that will not collide\n\n`const meta = Symbol(\"meta\")` is unique. `obj[meta] = \"hidden\"` does not show up in `Object.keys` or JSON by default.\n\n`Object.keys({ [Symbol(\"m\")]: 1 })` is `[]`. Symbols are skipped.\n\nThe desk pins a private note on a route card. The night log lists ordinary keys; the note stays off that list."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "keys-skip",
      "promptMd": "`Object.keys({ [Symbol(\"m\")]: 1 })` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "one",
          "md": "`[\"Symbol(m)\"]`"
        },
        {
          "id": "empty",
          "md": "`[]` — symbols are skipped"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "empty"
    },
    {
      "type": "check",
      "id": "keys-skip-sym",
      "kind": "cloze",
      "promptMd": "`Object.keys` on a symbol-only object is {{a}}.",
      "blanks": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "choices": [
            {
              "id": "[]",
              "md": "[]"
            },
            {
              "id": "[\"Symbol(m)\"]",
              "md": "[\"Symbol(m)\"]"
            },
            {
              "id": "[\"m\"]",
              "md": "[\"m\"]"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "a": "[]"
      },
      "explainMd": "Object.keys lists string keys. Symbol keys stay off that list unless you ask for them."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "hide-meta",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> Store `\"note\"` under a symbol key and print it (`note`).",
